flowchart TB
    accTitle: Door closer hardware
    accDescr: Power, motor drive and safety inputs from Fridge.drawio. This is a block diagram.
    %% PlatformIO C++ / FreeRTOS with MQTTS. The controller mounts on top of the fridge.
    %% Four fail-safes: limit switch ISR, INA219 stall cutoff, 8 s timeout and MQTTS abort.
    %% IR sensor at door seam stops forward drive when closed. Limit switch stops reverse drive at home.
    %% INA219 samples at 100 Hz. The controller retracts at ≥ 1200 mA.
    %% Driver supports PWM soft start and direction (PWMA 26, AIN1 27, AIN2 25).
    %% JGY-370 12 V 18 RPM worm gear drives a 3D-printed arm with rolling wheel.

    outlet["AC 220 V outlet"]
    adapter["12 V wall adapter"]
    jack["DC barrel jack"]
    buck["Mini buck converter"]
    door["D0 · KidBright32 / ESP32<br/>Local TLS MQTT and safety control"]
    ir["Close-range IR sensor<br/>Stops forward drive on closure"]
    limit["Limit switch<br/>Stops reverse drive at home"]
    ina["INA219 current sensor<br/>Stall cutoff ≥ 1200 mA"]
    driver["TB6612FNG motor driver"]
    motor["JGY-370 worm-gear motor"]

    outlet --> adapter
    adapter -->|"12 V"| jack
    jack -->|"12 V"| buck
    buck -->|"5 V"| door
    jack -->|"12 V"| ina
    ina -->|"12 V"| driver
    driver --> motor
    door -->|"PWM and direction"| driver
    door ---|"I2C1 · 0x40"| ina
    ir -->|"GPIO 32"| door
    limit -->|"GPIO 33 ISR"| door
